From 925125d03abd7fdb5e3510edfca9400fb8fc7bc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:38:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] Serve macOS 27's twin-layout textures, format 550 and
 heap queries

27's Setup Assistant creates textures tagged 12, whose descriptor carries
the level-0 layout twice, declares icon, panel and memoryless textures in
private format 550, and places textures in heaps after asking the device
for their size and alignment. Reims refused all three, and with no answer
to the heap query the guest placed every texture of a heap at one offset.

- A type-12 entry is served as type 3 once its descriptor drops the second
  copy of the layout.
- Format 550 is four bytes a texel and only ever rendered and sampled on
  the GPU; every wire decode stores it as BGRA8.
- On Linux, CmdHeapTextureSizeAndAlign is answered with rows padded to 256
  bytes, every level page-rounded, every slice, face and sample counted,
  aligned to 16 KiB: larger than the guest needs, never overlapping.

27.2's country panel loses the black frame and block it drew before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
